course: dictionary
lesson: 10575
title: Words that show a change of shape
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words describe a change from one shape to another, and uncurl is one of them. To uncurl means to open out or straighten from a curled shape. «Butterflies cannot chew: they uncurl a long tube called a proboscis to drink from orange slices.» The tube starts rolled up, so uncurl must mean it opens out ready for drinking.
explain: Use the clues around the word. The tube is rolled up, and the butterfly uses it to drink, so uncurl must mean straightening it out. Check your idea by swapping in "open out" for "uncurl". If the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
explain: The word also works with things you can hold. «Uncurl your fingers» means open your hand flat. A rolled-up poster uncurls when you smooth it out on the table.
fact: Uncurl is a verb. Its forms are uncurl, uncurls, uncurled and uncurling.
fact: The start "un-" often reverses an action, so uncurl is the opposite of curl.
fact: «Uncurl» means to open out or straighten from a curled shape.
fact: A hedgehog uncurls when it feels safe.
fact: Fern leaves uncurl in spring, and caterpillars and woodlice can uncurl too.
exercise: «Butterflies cannot chew: they uncurl a long tube called a proboscis to drink.» What does uncurl mean here? | To chew food into small bits | To paint with bright colours | To shut tightly and hide | *To open out or straighten from a curled shape
exercise: «Once the hedgehog feels safe, it uncurls and walks slowly away.» Which word is the opposite of uncurl? | *curl | walk | slowly | stretch
exercise: «The cat uncurled from her sleep and stretched.» What did the cat do? | Ran outside | Ate her dinner | Hid under the bed | *Straightened out from a curled-up ball
test: «Uncurl your fingers and show me your empty hands.» What does uncurl mean in this sentence? | *To straighten out, opening your hand flat | To hide | To close tightly | To knock on a door
test: «The rolled-up poster will uncurl when you put a book on each corner.» What happens to the poster? | It gets wet | It shuts into a tube | It catches fire | *It flattens and opens out
exam: «The fern leaves uncurl in spring, and the caterpillar uncurls slowly.» Which phrase best explains uncurl? | *To open out or straighten from a curled shape | To hide from a bird | To fall off a tree | To sing loudly
